From 48da886fc20dc8554d2f81493005d4939f58ed09 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Paul Scheduikat <luantak@pm.me>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 17:28:02 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] translate remaining obfuscation name contracts

Recognize obfuscated ABI address intrinsics, generic escape helpers,
and reflection receiver types and methods at their semantic boundaries.
Keep ABI wrapper liveness handling intact after renaming reflect
helpers, and resolve generic instantiation suffixes without changing
their arguments.

Translate embed, host-layout and reflection-header package identities.
Detect runtime/cgo through its mapped library path and preserve native
object policy so automatic internal links do not become external links.
Keep runtime sentinel and reflection-stub metadata hashed, with matching
runtime consumers, without weakening stack or garbage-collector checks.

Classify FIPS packages and symbols by their original semantic identity,
including frozen snapshots, while retaining integrity-section,
relocation and linkname-access checks.

The source baseline includes Garble's existing Go 1.27 patch series.
